class=site-content id=content><section
class=resources-single-large-banner style="background-image:url('https://workcare.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/iStock-458529435-scaled-e1745607501946.jpg');height: 478px;background-repeat: no-repeat;background-size: cover;"></section><section
class=resource-single-section><div
class=container><div
class=row><div
class="col col-12 d-flex justify-content-start"><div
class=resource-title><h1>First Aid for Thermal Burns – Monthly Tip for Injury Prevention</h1><div
class=resource-meta><p
class=date>January 15, 2025</p></div></div></div></div><div
class=row><div
class="col col-12 d-flex justify-content-between flex-wrap"><div
class=resource-sidebar><ul
class=category-list>
<li
class=text-uppercase>
<a
href=https://workcare.com/resources/wellness-tips/ aria-title="Read more Health + Wellness Tips">
Health + Wellness Tips	</a>
</li>
<li><a
href=https://workcare.com/resources/ aria-title="Read more resources">RESOURCES</a></li></ul><div
class=sidebar-search><form
method=get action=/resources/ class=resource-search-form>
<input
type=text name=_resource_search placeholder="Search Resources" value>
<button
type=submit><span
class=icon-search><img
width=17 height=17 src=/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/search-resource-form.png class=img-fluid></span></button></form></div><div
class=related-posts><p>RELATED POSTS</p><ul>
<li><a
href=https://workcare.com/resources/wellness-tips/office-ergonomics-tips-self-assessment-checklist/ >Office Ergonomics Tips + Self Assessment Checklist</a></li>
<li><a
href=https://workcare.com/resources/wellness-tips/first-aid-care-eye-injuries/ >First-aid Care: Eye Injuries</a></li>
<li><a
href=https://workcare.com/resources/wellness-tips/first-aid-care-reactions-to-extreme-temperatures/ >First-aid Care: Reactions to Extreme Temperatures</a></li></ul></div></div><div
class=resource-single><div
class=resource-excerpt><p>Thermal burns caused by contact with flames, hot liquid, steam, or super-heated objects are the most common type of work-related burns. Minor burns can be treated with first-aid remedies in most cases.</p></div><div
class=resource-content><p
class=wp-block-paragraph>The key is to act quickly and keep it simple.</p><p
class=wp-block-paragraph><strong>Tips</strong></p><ol
class=wp-block-list>
<li>For minor burns:</li></ol><p
class=wp-block-paragraph>•&nbsp; Run the burned area under cool, running water for 10-15 minutes; do not apply ice<br>•&nbsp; Use non-prescription burn cream and/or oral medication for pain and swelling<br>•&nbsp; Cover with a dry, non-stick sterile dressing to protect skin as it heals</p><ol
start=2 class=wp-block-list>
<li>If a blister forms, do not puncture or drain it. For a broken blister, clean with antibacterial soap and cool water, apply over-the-counter antibiotic ointment, and cover with dressing (as above).</li><li>Get care for signs of infection such as increased pain, redness, swelling, fever, or oozing.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></li></ol><p
class=wp-block-paragraph><strong>Did You Know?</strong></p><p
class=wp-block-paragraph>Burns can be prevented by being aware of workplace hazards and always taking precautions. A severe burn is a medical emergency. WorkCare’s onsite first responder, clinical care, and 24/7 telehealth teams provide guidance for the prevention and care of burns and other types of work-related injuries.</p><p
class=wp-block-paragraph></p><div
class=author-info><div
class=author-image><img
width=690 height=690 src=https://workcare.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Brandi-DeSerio-circle.png class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="Brandi DeSerio" decoding=async fetchpriority=high srcset="https://workcare.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Brandi-DeSerio-circle.png 690w, https://workcare.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Brandi-DeSerio-circle-300x300.png 300w, https://workcare.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Brandi-DeSerio-circle-150x150.png 150w" sizes="(max-width: 690px) 100vw, 690px"></div><div><h4 class="author-title">Brandi DeSerio</h4><p
class=author-introduction>Brandi DeSerio, BSN, RN, Occupational Health Nurse Trainer and Mentor at WorkCare</p></div></div></div></div><div
class=resource-social-icons><div
class=share-icons><ul>
<li><a
href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?url=https://workcare.com/resources/wellness-tips/first-aid-for-thermal-burns/&text=First Aid for Thermal Burns – Monthly Tip for Injury Prevention" target=_blank><img
